{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mbmc8cpTQWdJ25hZ2uLS4f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# wp1285 r5 — PROXIMA-P1-S3 optional manifest and publication\n2\t\n3\ttran_loi_goi_codex: ADR-0052@8ab100793df9831505f495543a74044b91c2c9ab\n4\ttran_kich_thuoc_sensitive: ADR-0053@8ab100793df9831505f495543a74044b91c2c9ab\n5\t\n6\t## Identity and authority\n7\t- packet_id: wp1285; revision: 5; mission: gh-1238; generation: 6.\n8\tOutcome and Mission graph remain unchanged: optional Proxima module manifest/SKILL plus a trustworthy pure-data manifest validation harness; exactly three new paths, sensitive, no activation. Depends on landed #1271/#1279.\n9\tOwner standing full scoped delegation and latest explicit instruction «Chuyển agy sang codex làm executore và reviewer. Reviewer chọn mô hình hoặc effort cao hơn» authorize this concrete r4 provider reroute and bounded replacement run. Preserve original r3/AGY artifacts and counters; no new Claude or AGY calls. This is not human code audit, code approval, finding waiver, cross-provider assurance or LIVE authority.\n10\tImmutable acceptance B=bf9914cb1a8e6f5047468f4d130b587015f8d73f/tree247971f6c723cc17de3632e4eaba2019545b356b; continuation H2=883d37826f443ce9301dd0bcd40cd5f97f1adf0e/tree8bb2149f025966ba09a351d5c60b5fd954d960b6. Historical H1=4196fbaaeb13b4d26d5f4f452b6c1a8b26150489 authorClaude1/run1c887f43, H2 actualClaude2/run52efda0981d24f4589b888e235a31f0e/session9e143387-f4f8-47be-a6f9-7995d8e6be6f terminal16:38:27Z before ownerAGY preference; both original handoffsNOT_RUN and all findings preserved. H2 has450adds/0del/3NEWpaths, no approval/productpush/PR/merge. B never moves through generation/provider changes.\n11\tNEW actual Executor openai_codex through codex CLI (lease enum codex/model_family openai/execution_surface codex_cli/transport machine), requested gpt-6.1-sol with model_reasoning_effort=high. Independent reviewer uses fresh Codex CLI gpt-6.1-sol with effort=xhigh, strictly higher effort, read-only separate clone/context, no fork/resume/context reuse. Per-run requested/observed model, effort, identity and unknowns retained. Both are same model family; assurance stays same_provider, never cross_approved. Protocol sensitive assurance/promotion gate stays HOLD pending an actually sufficient authorized audit; do not fabricate human audit, waive gate or merge merely from higher effort.\n12\tNEW independent cloud worker /workspace/scratch/wp1285-r4-g5-codex, branch agent/wp1285-r5-g6-codex, clean at H2, separate Git object store/index/refs (no alternates/hardlinks to ASUS). AGY g4 owner-cancel request targets only controller PID29460 with exact creation-time/executable/command identity; inability to measure stop is recorded UNKNOWN, never presumed dead. Revoke/quarantine g4 reciprocally before g5; stale ASUS workspace/output may not heartbeat/handoff/push into current generation. Do not import late AGY output or touch ASUS product files from new worker. Sole valid g5 writer only inside new cloud clone. Canonical unmodified launcher, workspace-write sandbox, approval never, fresh ephemeral CLI, explicit model/effort, absolute45min author deadline. Local source inspection/edit only exact3paths, no Git/tests/network/models/agents/LIVE/credential/profile/global config changes. No bypass flags; blocked handoff if permissions fail.\n13\tFresh independent actual Codex CLI requested gpt-6.1-sol/xhigh in new read-only clone/context reviews ENTIRE B..newH3/spec/security/F01 class after real native/Linux proofs. Actual writer/reviewer identities separate from GitHub submitter. Existing design advisory only historical input, not approval. Current canonical drift eefce7f is ops/land-only versus B, remeasure sources/policy/refs before new lease/model/merge.\n14\t\n15\t## Frozen write set and descriptor\n16\tExactly THREE NEW product paths; <=450 additions AND <=450 additions+deletions vsB under explicit ADR0053 opt-in; write set remains exactly THREE, not six:\n17\t- .agents/skills/proxima-control/scripts/ProximaControl.psd1\n18\t- .agents/skills/proxima-control/SKILL.md\n19\t- .agents/skills/proxima-control/tests/ProximaManifest.Tests.ps1\n20\tADR0053 opt-in gives room for readable seven-case/four-counterexample retained-artifact evidence without minifying the safety harness; canonical three-anchor ADR source verification required, not a custom waiver or blanket exemption.\n21\tClass sensitive. No S1/S2 module/wrapper/sample/test changes, no root SKILL/core/VERSION/release manifest/golden/workflow/launcher/ops product edits, no changelog fragment outside scope. Add-on is excluded from core Package by existing release exclusion; publication here means repository discoverability only, not installed/activated runtime.\n22\tCanonical change-impact policy/schema absent at B: NEW manual descriptor only for this r3 Packet/revision under owner full delegation; effective_write_set=three paths above, effective_review_class=sensitive, change_policy_sha=null, land_obligations=[]. Recheck presence/classifier/source/refs before lease/model/merge; policy appears or changes => recompute explicitly. Not an inherited waiver.\n23\t\n24\t## M1 — scripts/ProximaControl.psd1\n25\tA pure data manifest next to existing psm1. RootModule exactly ProximaControl.psm1; ModuleVersion exactly2.0.0; GUID fixed7f7055d6-51e3-4fb8-bbeb-7851a739bfb6; PowerShellVersion5.1; CompatiblePSEditions Desktop/Core. FunctionsToExport exactly Ordinal px and Invoke-ProximaOperation. CmdletsToExport/VariablesToExport/AliasesToExport empty arrays. Allow only these nine keys. No NestedModules, RequiredModules, ScriptsToProcess, RequiredAssemblies, TypesToProcess, FormatsToProcess or arbitrary code expressions. S1 dependency remains loaded only through unchanged S2 hash-before-import guard. No manifest expansion side effects.\n26\tMajor2 distinguishes changed public API from legacy installed module1.0.1 observed in P0; no claim existing host module was updated. Manifest loader must not silently replace another loaded module or reset session/selection. Do not modify wrapper/module to smooth over a conflict: document fail-closed behavior.\n27\t\n28\t## M2 — SKILL.md\n29\tFrontmatter name proxima-control, task-oriented description; version2.0.0 matches manifest. Concise practical Vietnamese instructions and headings covering Scope, Entry points, Target, WhatIf, Versions, Limits. Placeholder paths only; no real hostname/device IDs/config/credentials/profile paths. Show explicit repository-rooted wrapper and manifest import, ConfigPath/RepositoryRoot/TargetId for non-help; no defaults/autoconnect, PSCredential only when actually connecting. State is process-local, wrapper reuses exact sibling module only; mixed-entry invocation either preserves same module instance or gives ModuleConflict with no reset. Preserve explicit WhatIf/Confirm, no fallback/retry inference, Force never bypasses WhatIf.\n30\tDistinguish three identities: repo add-on2.0.0 + Gitcommit/tree; installed endpoint control module pair of source hashes from handshake; gateway binary runtime FileVersion NOT_MEASURED by S2/S3. status/models do not establish runtime version/quota/auth/upstream model identity. Runtime FileVersion measurement belongs to P4 observation, not silently added to S2. No activation, endpoint/service/account/profile changes in S3. Standalone optional add-on does not install itself or enter core Package; removing it leaves core intact. OutputAI/web is untrusted data; verified legal quotations follow root SKILL/source verification. Link doctrine instead of copying protocol paragraphs; doctrine-scan applies. Include ordinary no-inference examples and installation/unload boundaries, supported PS5.1/7 and snapshot/hash-import/listener-query race/realWinRM limitations.\n31\t\n32\t## M3 — tests/ProximaManifest.Tests.ps1\n33\tSelf-contained no Pester/newdependency; params AddonRoot, ScratchRoot, ReportPath, Counterexamples switch. Evidence outside repo and outside cleanup scope; fresh process per baseline/candidate runtime. Report all SEVEN stable normal IDs PM01..PM07 with outcomes/reasons, actual count, API/manifest absence vs setup errors, runtime/edition/head or source hashes, cleanup and preserved evidence paths; rc0 all pass, rc1 property failure, rc2 setup failure. Baseline B lacks both new publication files: still report all seven RED MANIFEST_ABSENT/SKILL_ABSENT with actualrc1, not zero-test/setup error. Candidate actual7/7 and rc0 on both nativePS5.1/7. Harness never mutates actual installed modules/gateway/user config/profile or unrelated modules/resources; use owned isolated fixture roots and dummy config. Import/calls only help/config/WhatIf and private copies; no real network/service/session/credential prompts.\n34\tPM01 maps M1: AST parses exactly one hashtable data expression with no executable statements/parse errors. Use parser SafeGetValue/AST checks, no dependence on unavailable Import-PowerShellDataFile. No evaluating arbitrary manifest code.\n35\tPM02 maps M1: exact allow-list keys/types/fixedGUID/RootModule/PS metadata and Ordinal declared export arrays/version; wildcards explicitly invalid even when unchanged S2 ExportModuleMember would hide them empirically.\n36\tPM03 maps M1: actual Test-ModuleManifest and fresh native process Import-Module manifest succeeds, exactly two actual exports, px help positive. Capture actual ModuleInfo.Path/version and runtime; empty exports/no execution is not pass.\n37\tPM04 maps M1: private-copy tampered ProximaConfig.psm1 must be rejected with named DependencyMismatch BEFORE its harmless sentinel side effect; preserve original fixture/report/output and verify original source unchanged. Do not run untrusted code just to get a kill.\n38\tPM05 maps M2: manifest and documented version match both directions, required structural headings and name/description present, three version domains and placeholder/example targets consistent. Not merely absence of an 