ables, conversions, attributes, using statements, executable blocks and other non-allowlisted AST forms cannot reach SchemaOk.\",\n86\t        \"The permitted enum modes do not introduce an execution route: named block placement is constrained by root and child-edge checks, and StringConstantExpressionAst remains literal data. Optional parser properties are reflected rather than directly accessed under PS5.1 StrictMode.\",\n87\t        \"Ordinary literal strings, arrays and comments remain compatible with the permitted data shape; exact nine-key, type, value and Ordinal export checks remain after SafeGetValue.\"\n88\t      ],\n89\t      \"verified_positive_controls\": [\n90\t        \"Native PS5.1 and PS7 candidate PM01–PM07: 7/7, rc0, no setup errors.\",\n91\t        \"Native counterexample parents: 12/12 on each runtime, including CX00 positive controls.\",\n92\t        \"Eight retained runtime/tamper pairs independently checked for actual manifest import, two exports, px help, same module object, intact sentinel and DependencyMismatch before sentinel execution.\",\n93\t        \"Unchanged S2 normal regression: 26/26 on each runtime.\"\n94\t      ],\n95\t      \"verified_negative_controls\": [\n96\t        \"Six named-end/end-clean/background probes: actual rc1, named PM01 rejection, runtime_children=0, PM04 NOT_EXECUTED, no setup errors.\",\n97\t        \"PS5.1 clean/background syntax receives parser rejection; no unsupported-syntax behavioral credit claimed.\",\n98\t        \"PS7 background-only rollback removes exactly the new Background rejection while retaining its property continue and all other H3 checks. PM01 then passes and runtime_children=2. Overall rc1 arises later and is not credited as a before-import kill.\"\n99\t      ],\n100\t      \"rollback_mutant_sha256\": \"1c73439c657c671a11c7e1759593e4df4871e7a2de3bdf8c84411f7e00cc36a0\",\n101\t      \"remaining_manifestations\": [],\n102\t      \"closure_basis\": \"Independent whole-class source analysis pl